  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "Type_ProfileSequenceId_Write",
    "file": "lcms/src/cmstypes.c",
    "description": "Heap OOB read occurs when writing a profileSequenceId tag because Type_ProfileSequenceId_Write trusts Seq->n and passes it to WritePositionTable/WriteSeqID without validating that the backing Seq allocation actually contains that many entries. WriteSeqID then reads Seq->seq[n].Description/ProfileID past the allocated cmsSEQ object (crash at cmstypes.c:3522 in SaveDescription argument fetch).",
    "conditions": "In cms_profile_fuzzer, attacker-controlled ICC is opened, cmsReadTag(hProfile, cmsSigGamutTag) mutates/loads tag data, then cmsSaveProfileToFile serializes all tags. A malformed profile can produce an inconsistent cmsSEQ (count field larger than allocated seq array). During save, SaveTags -> Type_ProfileSequenceId_Write iterates Seq->n entries and triggers out-of-bounds access in WriteSeqID. Input must include a psid tag (profileSequenceIdType) with crafted count/structure so in-memory seq length and Seq->n diverge."
  },
